# Build context hygiene, plus one deliberate leak guard.
#
# corpus/processed can hold REAL captured archive content on disk (`make sync`
# pulls it from camden) even though it is gitignored and never committed - see
# README.md's Content warning and .gitignore's own corpus guard. If it exists on
# the machine running `docker build .`, it must never enter the build context, or
# it could reach an image layer and ship real conversation content inside an
# image forever. The Dockerfile's builder stage only COPYs cmd/ and internal/
# anyway, so this is belt-and-braces, not load-bearing - but the belt costs
# nothing and the braces are exactly the failure mode worth not trusting to a
# single Dockerfile COPY line staying correct forever.
/corpus/
/corpus.sig.json
shapes*.json
*.profile.json
*.jsonl
*.jsonl.gz
*.jsonl.zst

.git
.github
docs
testdata

/bin
/dist
config.yaml
.env
*.md
